15 0 obj
<<
/A 44 0 R
/Alt (Flowchart depicting a process from Baseline State to Normal State. lt shows three stages: Baseline State labeled "initial state," Post-Treatment State with "state-specific utility varies by treatment," and Normal State labeled "absorbing state." Transitions include Treatment Initiation leading to Post-Treatment State, then Linear Recovery to 60 days, ending at Normal State.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 32 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
16 0 obj
<<
/A 44 0 R
/Alt (The tornado diagram presents deterministic sensitivity analysis comparing TM+BZDs versus WL. The model was most sensitive to variations in the weighted average treatment duration of TM, followed by the weighted average treatment duration of WL and average winning bid price of WL. Changes in PSQI score reductions had comparatively smaller impacts on the incremental cost-effectiveness ratio \(ICER\).)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 36 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
17 0 obj
<<
/A 44 0 R
/Alt (The tornado diagram presents deterministic sensitivity analysis comparing WL versus BLM. The model was most sensitive to variations in the reduction difference in PSQI scores for SQWWZ against both BLM and WL, followed by the weighted average treatment duration of BLM and WL.  Changes in the average winning bid price and daily dosage of the interventions had comparatively smaller impacts on the incremental cost-effectiveness ratio \(ICER\).)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 37 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
18 0 obj
<<
/A 44 0 R
/Alt (The tornado diagram presents deterministic sensitivity analysis comparing SQWWZ versus BLM. The model was most sensitive to variations in the weighted average treatment duration of BLM and  SQWWZ, followed by the average winning bid price per unit of BLM. Changes in PSQI score reductions had a more moderate impact on the incremental cost-effectiveness ratio \(ICER\).)
/K 1
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 37 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
19 0 obj
<<
/A 44 0 R
/Alt (The tornado diagram presents deterministic sensitivity analysis comparing TM+BZDs versus SQWWZ. The model was most sensitive to variations in the weighted average daily dosage and average winning bid price per unit of SQWWZ, followed by its treatment duration. Parameters related to BZD and TM Oral Liquid, as well as the reduction difference in PSQI scores, had a more moderate impact on the incremental cost-effectiveness ratio \(ICER\).)
/K 2
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 37 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
20 0 obj
<<
/A 44 0 R
/Alt (Scatter plot showing Incremental Costs on the Y-axis and Incremental QALYs on the X-axis with numerous blue data points clustered around the center. An orange dashed line indicates an willingness-to-pay threshold.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 38 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
21 0 obj
<<
/A 44 0 R
/Alt (Line graph showing cost-effectiveness probability against willingness-to-pay in Chinese yuan. The orange line \(WL\) begins at a high probability but shows a steady decline, whereas the blue line \(TM + BZD\) starts low and demonstrates a consistent upward trend. A notable intersection between the two curves occurs within the first half of the graph.)
/K 1
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 38 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
22 0 obj
<<
/A 44 0 R
/Alt (Line graph showing cost-effectiveness probability against willingness-to-pay in Chinese yuan. The blue line \(SQWWZ\) starts high and decreases sharply, while the orangeline \(BLM\) starts low and increases sharply, crossing near the middle.)
/K 0
/P 7 0 R
/Pg 39 0 R
/S /Figure
/T (Figure)
>>
endobj
